1	//! `copy_pieces` — a clip's pieces between given project times copied onto
2	//! another track at the same times (road map "creator-jobs" SW1, spec §11
3	//! SW-11, SW-12). It is the primitive Clip ▸ Switch Angle ▸ writes with: a
4	//! piece of a synced angle shows the angle's own frame at every time.
5	//!
6	//! A piece is EXACTLY the middle a `split` at its two ends would leave —
7	//! its source window, a ramp's map and rate, its actions clipped, a
8	//! graphic's `in` and `length`, its words rebased — because it is made by
9	//! `edit_split.rs`'s `split_clip` itself, on a scratch copy holding only the
10	//! source clip. This module states none of those rules; it only says where
11	//! the middle lands: a fresh id and fresh action ids from the result's own
12	//! counter, `track` the destination, `start` the range's start, no
13	//! transition and no link, and `enabled` overridden where `video`/`audio`
14	//! are given.
15	//!
16	//! In order (SW-11): `Err` for an unknown clip, then for an unknown track;
17	//! each pair put in order and snapped, a range empty on the grid dropped
18	//! (nothing left is an identity), the rest sorted by start; then the
19	//! refusals — a nest clip, a range outside the clip, overlapping ranges, a
20	//! locked destination, a destination holding a clip over a range. The exit
21	//! is `finish`.
22	
23	use crate::edit_clip::clip_end;
24	use crate::edit_split::split_clip;
25	use crate::edit_time::locked_track;
26	use crate::model::{Clip, Project, Source};
27	use crate::outcome::Outcome;
28	use crate::time::Ticks;
